MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The heat shrink tubing feels like a useful next purchase because it would insulate and protect connections made with the crimp terminals I bought.",
    "The removable fastening tape and repair epoxy connect with my duct tape and vinyl cement purchases: they offer other ways to secure or repair things when the materials and task suit them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The temperature guns, sound meter, and caliper are plausible workshop tools, but I have no specific measurement task that makes me want them now.",
    "Locking nuts, pocket-hole screws, and the wire brush require a particular repair, woodworking project, or compatible tool; buying clamps and adhesives does not establish those needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair-supply purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop equipment, even when it serves a different purpose.",
    "The two temperature guns repeat the same unsupported assumption that I currently need to check surface temperatures."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A clear connection to supplies I already bought matters: protecting my electrical connections is a stronger reason to buy than simply being another repair-related product.",
    "My purchases span several years, so an older purchase is a clue to possible usefulness, not proof of an active project. I need a concrete use, suitable materials, and compatibility before choosing specialized supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical fastening and repair supplies but stretched it into specialized tools without a clear current use."
}
